<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices down on poor demand.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices down on poor demand.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices fell slightly in central Indian markets on limited demand from processing plants, dealers said.</p>
<p>Prices fell by 50 rupees per tonne while arrivals were at around 15,000 tonnes, unchanged from Wednesday, they said.</p>
<p>They said demand from processing plants was poor due to a funds crunch and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent prices improved by 100 rupees per tonne while soyoil refined prices were steady in limited trade, they said.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were firm with Chicago Board of Trade (CBT) quoted at $231.60. Soymeal yellow was $266-267 per tonne in export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was $135 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,600 rupees FOR Bedibunder and 4,550-4,575 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
